      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "The search began with the formulation of the following research question by R.S.C., whose clinical response was possible, in PIO (Population-Intervention-Outcome) format [46]: 'Has the possible exposure to SARS-CoV-2 during the COVID-19 pandemic (I) affected the mental health (O) of HPs providing health care outside the hospital (P)?",
      "reason": "The provided evidence frames the question around exposure and outcomes rather than planned intervention-effect comparisons; no planned comparisons are described as would be expected for intervention-effects reviews."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 72
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "The selected research studies had to meet the following inclusion criteria: (1) being original, (2) based on qualitative and/or quantitative methods, (3) with any methodological design, (4) submitted for peer-review, (5) published in English, Spanish, French, Italian or Portuguese, (6) completed after December 2019, (7) without geographic limitation, (8) with at least the abstract available, and (9) that in their results evaluated the impact of possible exposure to SARS-CoV-2 on levels of stress, anxiety, depression and/or self-efficacy of the HPs who were working in public, private, or voluntary out-of-hospital EMS during the COVID-19 pandemic or identified factors related positively or negatively with these levels or compared them with those obtained in other working environments and/or professional categories.",
      "reason": "Inclusion criteria are specified (study characteristics, outcomes/eligibility focus, designs/methods, and out-of-hospital EMS setting). However, the evidence does not clearly specify any follow-up requirements for eligibility."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "The selected research studies had to meet the following inclusion criteria: ... (4) submitted for peer-review, (5) published in English, Spanish, French, Italian or Portuguese, (6) completed after December 2019, (7) without geographic limitation, (8) with at least the abstract available ...",
      "reason": "Report characteristics relevant to eligibility are specified, including peer-review/report status (“submitted for peer-review”), dissemination language, and a date restriction (“completed after December 2019”)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The evidence describes reasons for exclusion (e.g., unrelated to the objective, publication format, no data from out-of-hospital HPs, low methodological quality), but it does not explicitly distinguish exclusion due to outcomes not being measured vs outcomes not being reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The evidence does not describe groups used in each synthesis or how such groups are linked to specific comparisons/objectives. It states that an 'Anarrative synthesis' was performed, but no synthesis grouping structure tied to comparisons is reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Opinion articles and editorials, studies of low scientific-technical quality, those that did not reply to the posed research question and/or were not in line with the objective of the review, as well as others that, despite including out-of-hospital HPs, contributed no specific data on this subgroup in their results were excluded.",
      "reason": "The evidence provides rationales for notable eligibility restrictions by stating why specific types of studies (e.g., editorials/opinions, low-quality studies, not answering the question/not aligned with objective, and those lacking subgroup data) were excluded."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 74
}

